#
# Counter-example for the native math:ExactPreservationViolated gate: a
# math:JointProbabilityTable (which declares logic:ExactPreservation at the TBox level)
# tabulates two logic:jointOutcome rows whose logic:jointProbability values (0.5 and
# 0.4) sum to 0.9 ≠ 1. The native gate sums the mass by exact-rational arithmetic and
# MUST emit math:ExactPreservationViolated (and no other probability failure class).
# The table has outcomes, so math:IncompleteDependencyModel does NOT also fire.
# Back-reference: math:JointProbabilityTable / math:ExactPreservationViolated (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:overclaimedTable a math:JointProbabilityTable ;
    logic:jointOutcome ex:outcomeA , ex:outcomeB .

ex:outcomeA logic:jointProbability 0.5 .
ex:outcomeB logic:jointProbability 0.4 .
